Z||000000||BAM-BAM||12-17-2000||02:44 AM||||  I just installed my new headliner. When I went to install the visor hangers, I got them mixed up, now I'm not sure how to get them aligned. Is there anyone out there who knows this little secret? TIA<P><BR> Peace, B2 OUT! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||8
Z||000001||theogre||12-17-2000||01:44 PM||||The visor hardware doesn't care what side of the car you mount it on. The same hardware is in both visors. The only thing that makes a diferance is the presence of pockets, label, and vanity mirrors.<P>simply rotate the mounting plate untill the visor lines up with the pocket in the light assembly. You only have 3 choices. One corner of the plate is higher than the otheres. This is the one that points towards you.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||12-17-2000||01:59 PM|||| I noticed that the triangle has three unequal sides, thus I believe there must be a directional delima that I need to desipher. Thank Ogre, I'll keep working on it.<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||12-17-2000||05:50 PM||||<B>YOU CAN DO IT</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Ogre's right though.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||12-17-2000||07:36 PM||||yep, Ogre's right. It seems like this happens to me every time we have a car in the shop that I put a headliner in!! There is only one way they can go where the visor will hang level from the bracket the the dome light housing -- keep rotating that triangular bracket until the visor sits as it should.....by the way, it is far easier to pre-drill the holes in the headliner before putting it in the car - I guess I shouldn't be telling you that now tho, huh? shhhhhhh.......||||reg||1
